IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-24.l4 -- ARTICLE 24: RESPONSIBILITY OF THE CONTROLLER.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Whose duty: the controller's (24(1) first sentence, 24(2)); 24(1) second sentence is passive ("Those measures
-- shall be reviewed and updated") and names no party, so it is a decision function only.  The data subject (and any
-- supervisory authority) may rely on it.  24(3) is a permission about evidence ("may be used as an element").
-- Borrowed (plain inputs): approved codes of conduct (Art 40, P4) and approved certification mechanisms (Art 42, P4).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 24(1) matter taken into account` IS ONE OF
    `Art 24(1) the nature of the processing`
    `Art 24(1) the scope of the processing`
    `Art 24(1) the context of the processing`
    `Art 24(1) the purposes of the processing`
    `Art 24(1) the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons`

DECLARE `Art 24(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 24(1) implement appropriate technical and organisational measures`

DECLARE `Art 24(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 24(2) implement appropriate data protection policies`

§ `Article 24(1), first sentence`

-- src:310 | 1. Taking into account the nature, scope, context and purposes of processing as well as the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons, the controller shall implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure and to be able to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation. Those measures shall be reviewed and updated where necessary.
@ref Art 24(1), first sentence (src:310)
GIVEN `the matters the controller took into account` IS A LIST OF `Art 24(1) matter taken into account`
      `appropriate technical and organisational measures are implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures ensure that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures make it possible to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 24(1) the controller implements appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure and to be able to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation` MEANS
    IF     elem `Art 24(1) the nature of the processing` `the matters the controller took into account`
       AND elem `Art 24(1) the scope of the processing` `the matters the controller took into account`
       AND elem `Art 24(1) the context of the processing` `the matters the controller took into account`
       AND elem `Art 24(1) the purposes of the processing` `the matters the controller took into account`
       AND elem `Art 24(1) the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons` `the matters the controller took into account`
       AND `appropriate technical and organisational measures are implemented`
       AND `the measures ensure that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation`
       AND `the measures make it possible to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Taking into account the nature, scope, context and purposes of processing as well as the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons, the controller shall implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure and to be able to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation."

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: no time limit, no consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
@ref Art 24(1), first sentence, regulative form (src:310-310)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 24(1) action`
`Art 24(1) the controller must implement appropriate technical and organisational measures` MEANS
    PARTY `controller`
    MUST `Art 24(1) implement appropriate technical and organisational measures`
    HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 24(1) the controller must implement appropriate technical and organisational measures` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 24(1) implement appropriate technical and organisational measures` AT 20
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 24(1) the controller must implement appropriate technical and organisational measures` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline, so no breach).

§ `Article 24(1), second sentence: review`

-- src:310 | 1. Taking into account the nature, scope, context and purposes of processing as well as the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons, the controller shall implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure and to be able to demonstrate that processing is performed in accordance with this Regulation. Those measures shall be reviewed and updated where necessary.
@ref Art 24(1), second sentence (src:310)
GIVEN `reviewing and updating the measures is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures have been reviewed and updated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 24(1) the measures are reviewed and updated where necessary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reviewing and updating the measures is necessary`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "where"): "Those measures shall be reviewed and updated where necessary."
        IF `the measures have been reviewed and updated`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Those measures shall be reviewed and updated where necessary."

§ `Article 24(2): data protection policies`

-- src:311 | 2. Where proportionate in relation to processing activities, the measures referred to in paragraph 1 shall include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller.
@ref Art 24(2) (src:311)
GIVEN `implementing data protection policies is proportionate in relation to the processing activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 24(2) the measures include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`implementing data protection policies is proportionate in relation to the processing activities`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where proportionate in relation to processing activities, the measures referred to in paragraph 1 shall include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller."
        IF `the measures include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "the measures referred to in paragraph 1 shall include the implementation of appropriate data protection policies by the controller"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: gated by "Where proportionate"; no time limit, no consequence.
@ref Art 24(2), regulative form (src:311-311)
GIVEN `implementing data protection policies is proportionate in relation to the processing activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 24(2) action`
`Art 24(2) the controller must implement appropriate data protection policies where proportionate` MEANS
    IF `implementing data protection policies is proportionate in relation to the processing activities`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         MUST `Art 24(2) implement appropriate data protection policies`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 24(2) the controller must implement appropriate data protection policies where proportionate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 24(2) implement appropriate data protection policies` AT 9
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 24(2) the controller must implement appropriate data protection policies where proportionate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline, so no breach).

§ `Article 24(3): codes of conduct and certification`

-- src:312 | 3. Adherence to approved codes of conduct as referred to in Article 40 or approved certification mechanisms as referred to in Article 42 may be used as an element by which to demonstrate compliance with the obligations of the controller.
@ref Art 24(3) (src:312)
GIVEN `the controller adheres to an approved code of conduct as referred to in Article 40` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller adheres to an approved certification mechanism as referred to in Article 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 24(3) adherence may be used as an element by which to demonstrate compliance with the obligations of the controller` MEANS
    IF `the controller adheres to an approved code of conduct as referred to in Article 40`
       OR `the controller adheres to an approved certification mechanism as referred to in Article 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text names adherence to approved codes of conduct and approved certification mechanisms; it does not say that nothing else may be used, or that these are not enough
